  "historical_output_text": " Describe the weather pattern of a heatwave in simple terms.\n\nA heatwave is when a place experiences abnormally hot weather for a week or more. This happens when a big area of very warm air moves in and stays over a region. Usually, hot air rises up into the atmosphere and then sinks back down again. But in a heatwave, a high pressure area forms. This acts like a dome that traps the warm air near the surface and stops it from rising. The dome also pushes away clouds and storms that could bring cooler rain. So the warm air stays trapped near the ground and heats up even more in the sunshine. That",
